    "reply": "Clinical evaluations for the variant record document assertions spanning not-provided, protective, likely-benign, pathogenic, and other [1]. The available findings associate this locus with specific sequence designations and related identifiers from the literature, although they do not explicitly name a specific medical condition [1][2]. \n\n## Clinical Significance Assertions\nThe variant record includes reports of multiple clinical significance categories, including pathogenic classifications alongside protective and likely-benign interpretations [1]. Additional reported classifications for the variant encompass other as well as not-provided entries [1].\n\n## Associated Sequence Identifiers\nLiterature annotations associate the variant with the nucleotide change c.20A>T [2]. Another associated literature variant representation is c.-50T>C [5].\n\n## Related Variation Identifiers\nThe literature evidence also references the identifier rs334348 [3]. Furthermore, the records link this variation to rs334353 [4]. An additional associated identifier in the findings is rs334773 [6].",
